{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And this that Scripture says <b>as they journeyed from the east</b> is a sign that the mountains of Ararat are in the east." "And the sense of <b>and they found a plain</b>: they sought a good place to build a city, until they found this plain. And the meaning of בקעה is a level valley, the opposite of mountains and ridges (Isaiah 40:4), and likewise \"like cattle in the valley it goes down\" (Isaiah 63:14). And it is possible that it is between mountains, as though cloven within."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:06.369637672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}